# Canonical documentation ownership

Authority model: `docs/CANONICAL_OWNERSHIP.md`.

## Canonical sources (do not duplicate)

| Domain | Canonical file |
|--------|----------------|
| Execution order / phases | `docs/ROADMAP.md` |
| Shipped stages 4G–4V | `docs/MASTER_PLAN.md` |
| Architecture | `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` |
| State lifecycles | `docs/governance/STATE_MACHINES.md` |
| Policies / invariants | `docs/governance/*` |
| Enforcement map | `docs/governance/ENFORCEMENT_MATRIX.md` |
| Ops history | `docs/PROJECT_LOG.md` (historical, immutable log) |
| ADR lifecycle | `docs/adr/ADR_LIFECYCLE.md` |

## Conflict resolution order

1. Runtime behavior (code + env on `/opt/scrap`)
2. Canonical doc for that domain
3. Governance policy
4. Secondary references
5. PROJECT_LOG / historical notes

## Forbidden

- Duplicate runtime truths across multiple docs
- Duplicate state machine or roadmap definitions (link instead)
- Treat PROJECT_LOG as current policy
- Implement from ADR in `proposed` state as if accepted

## On doc changes

Update **canonical source first**, then links/references only.
